    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d747">

                <pb facs="0978" n="876" xml:id="pg876"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/3213: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-12-23T15:00:00-05:00">December 23,
                            1935—3 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>398. Your 639, December 21, 4 p.m. You should immediately communicate orally with
                    the Foreign Office and confirm by note as follows:</p>
                <p>With regard to the suggestion contained in the Foreign Office note under
                    reference, in pursuit of its uniform policy from the beginning of the
                    Italo-Ethiopian Controversy of pursuing its own separate and independent course
                    with respect to all phases of the matter—the American Government must reserve
                    its most-favored-nation rights and its position with regard to any injury to
                    American trade arising out of this or any similar arrangement which the British
                    Government may enter into even though they be only of brief duration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Carr</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
